Z||000000||Seanh||11-20-2000||09:14 PM||||Sorry for the stupid question, but I am unclean if I use the vacuum lines under the plenum on the new engine? I need a new set for the GT, but I will just get a used set of plastic ones if I dont need them on the new engine, but if I do use them, I want to get Rodneys steel set. Thanks<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/transsig.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://www.kdsi.net/~sean" TARGET=_blank>Sean's Fiero Page</A><BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8 Auto<BR>Going on to 3.4 in Jan.<BR><I>"If you smoke after sex, you're doing it way to fast".</I>||||reg||1
Z||000001||mrfiero||11-20-2000||09:35 PM||||No stupid questions......Yes, you need the vacuum lines.  Just picture the 3.4 as a 2.8.....use everything the 2.8 needed and you'll do just fine.||||reg||1
